From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:30:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/25] [GLM5Next] Read exact BF16 mHC weights in the fused
 decode kernel

GLM-5.3-Flash keeps its 2 x 45 mHC projections (hc_attn_fn, hc_ffn_fn,
[24, 4 * hidden]) as FP32 parameters, but the checkpoint stores them in
BF16. The fused post + pre-norm decode kernel (mhc_fused_tilelang, up
to 32 tokens) re-reads the whole 1.5 MiB FP32 matrix for every token.

- tilelang_kernels.py: mhc_fused_bf16w_tilelang is the stock kernel with
  a BF16 weight_t, widened to FP32 in the FMA, plus its launcher.
  The stock FP32 kernel is unchanged; DeepSeek-V4 keeps using it.
- tilelang.py: register_mhc_bf16_weights() keeps a BF16 copy of each
  FP32 weight that BF16 represents exactly, keyed by data_ptr, and
  mhc_fused_post_pre_tilelang uses the BF16 kernel for those. Before
  registering anything it runs both kernels on one weight at 1, 3, 16
  and 32 tokens and registers nothing unless every output matches
  bit for bit.
- GLM registers its weights after load_weights and warms the kernel up.

Numerics: widening BF16 to FP32 is exact, and the copies exist only for
weights whose FP32 values are BF16 values, so each FMA sees the same
operands in the same order. Sinkhorn and the larger-batch DeepGEMM path
still read the FP32 weights, so the copies add ~71 MiB per rank.
VLLM_GLM53_MHC_BF16W=0 turns it off. The copies are keyed by data_ptr
and refreshed by load_weights, so a reload that changes hc_*_fn in place
without load_weights would leave them stale.

Source: kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 @ c748079,
  experimental/fixes/tilelang_kernels.py and mhc_tilelang.py (base vLLM
  ddd6fbca), by Matt Mastracci; porting authorized by the owner. The
  exactness gate and the bitwise self-check follow
  knapcio/GLM-5.3-Flash-4x-DGX-Spark-TP4 @ 770d115,
  overlay/glm_mhc_bf16w.py (MIT), re-implemented here. Kindling's
  VLLM_MHC_FUSED_MAX_TOKENS knob is not ported.
Upstream: absent in v0.31.0 and main.
Claimed gain: Kindling (4x GB10, TP=4): 8.2 us per call instead of
  11.9, ~1% faster decode at one stream, greedy logprobs identical to
  the FP32 path. knapcio (4x GB10, TP=4): warm kernel 6.7 us at M=4 and
  16.9 us at M=16 before; part of a decode set worth -1.90 ms per c1
  step together; bitwise identical at M=1..16.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
